The new command is not wired into the Windows/MSVC source generation path, so a supported CI build will fail to link. The AutoEDA artifacts also leave the completed stmap0 iteration unaudited and include transient process state.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Wire stmap0 into the Windows source list — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/module.make:69-69
  This only adds `abcStmap_0.c` to the make-based source list. The Windows CI generates `abclib.vcxproj` from `abclib.dsp`, which still does not list `src\base\abci\abcStmap_0.c`; with `abc.c` now registering `Abc_CommandStmap0`, that job will link `abc.c` without the implementation and fail with an unresolved external.

- [P2] Record stmap0 in the canonical version log — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:1-4
  The change includes a `stmap0` implementation and benchmark/CEC artifacts, but the canonical version log is still just the scaffold header. Under the campaign contract, each completed numbered variant needs its hypothesis, validation, benchmark results, correctness, review disposition, commit, and next-step entry, otherwise this iteration cannot be audited or counted by the `version_log_updated` gate.

- [P3] Exclude live supervisor PID state from the commit — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/launch.pid:1-1
  If the untracked runtime tree is added as-is, this file commits the local supervisor PID (`10382`) along with the matching lock state. That is transient machine-local process state, not a reproducible artifact, and a restored workspace can treat the stale PID/lock as an active campaign owner or block/restart incorrectly.
